[[File:E 047.png|thumb|[[Metal Hippoe|Metal Hippoe]], the first example of a Metal enemy]]
'''Metal Enemies''' (Japanese: メタルな敵 ''Metaruna Teki'') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]]. Metal enemies have surprisingly low health compared to enemies of the same caliber, which is offset by them only taking 1 damage from all attacks (even with Strong, Massive or Insane Damage), except for [[Critical Hit]]s/[[The Cat God (Special Cat)|Wrath of God]], the [[Ototo Corps#Waterblast|Waterblast]], and [[:Category:Metal Killer Cats|Metal Killers]]' attacks. Critical Hits and [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|Wrath of God]] ignore the Metal ability completely, dealing full damage (including the 2x multiplier of a Critical Hit), while Waterblast and Metal Killers take off a set percentage of Metal enemies' current HP with each hit. Metal enemies are typically short-ranged aggressive pushers with a fast attack rate, and only a handful of units can use abilities on them. Using [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitters]] is the most reliable way to deal with them, but spamming fast attackers is an alternative against weaker Metals.

See [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Metal abilities.

*Anti-Metal abilities are improved by the [[Titanium Fruit]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]].
*The only Metal [[Talent Orbs]] are Defense Up Orbs, which can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Metal|Steel Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Metal|Steel Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Metal|Steel Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Adamantine Dawn]], [[Adamantine Apex]], [[Adamantine Refuge]]

==Trivia==
*Almost all Metal enemies have entirely green eyes.
*There are no Metal enemies with another trait.
*Metal is the only trait without an [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]], [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], or [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]].
*In [[Nyanko Defence Force]], [[Jackie Peng]] had [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]], [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and Metal variants that have not appeared in other games.
*Metal was the only trait from [[The Battle Cats]] to also appear in [[Yuru-i GeGeGe no Kitarou: Youkai Dotabata Daisensou|YuruGeGe]].
**Metals in YuruGeGe could have multiple traits, but retain their resilience to non-critical attacks, some examples being [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%A5%C9%A5%ED%A5%BF%A5%DC%A1%BC%A5%B0Dk-2 Dorotaborg Dk-2] (a Serious/Metal variant of [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Dorotabō|Dorotabō]]) and [https://seesaawiki.jp/urugege/d/%bb%e0%c5%b4%b5%b4 Shitetsuki] (a Metal/Death variant of an [[wikia:gegegenokitaro:Oni|Oni]]).
**All Metals in YuruGeGe had yellow lightbulbs for eyes, along with a blinking red light just like [[Metal Doge]]'s tail on their head.
*Metal had a direct equivalent in [[Kyoutou Project]]: Steel, which was essentially Metal under a different name.
*All Metal enemies with descriptions are variants of already-existing enemies.
**Metal is the only trait where this is the case.

